              "text": "انوکھا (anokhā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from anapekṣa, \"careless\" (CDIAL 289). It is built on apekṣā, \"consideration, expectation\": what is strange is what nobody expected."
